    <string name="about_app_text">Npltz is a clean Nepali (Bikram Sambat) calendar for Android, built with Java and Material 3. It shows BS dates with an AD side view, a live greeting and Nepal time, home-screen widgets, daily reminders, a permanent date notification, and reminders for events and special days.\n\nNpltz started as a TUI app for desktop and Termux. This Android app is a native rebuild that shares the same calendar logic and design language, now built around Material 3 components and a Material You color system.\n\nEverything runs offline. The BS calendar data is compiled into the app, so there is no API, no account, no ads, no analytics, and no tracking. You open it, use it, and close it.\n\nBikram Sambat data is included up to 2090 BS. Data beyond that is not reliably available yet, so the app will be updated once accurate data is out.</string>

